---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About ChemistryDesk | Research-Grade Benchtop Computational Suite"
  description="Learn about ChemistryDesk, an open scientific utility suite developed by physical and analytical chemists to eliminate benchtop volumetric errors and provide standardized stoichiometric workflows."
>
  <main style="max-width: 900px; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #1e293b; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;">
    
    <!-- Hero / Mission -->
    <div style="border-bottom: 2px solid #e2e8f0; padding-bottom: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <span style="display: inline-block; background: #e0f2fe; color: #0284c7; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 9999px; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        Scientific Precision &amp; Transparency
      </span>
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">
        About ChemistryDesk
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #475569; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
        A research-grade computational suite developed to bridge the gap between theoretical stoichiometry and practical wet-lab formulation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial & Scientific Authority -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Editorial Leadership &amp; Scientific Background
      </h2>
      <p>
        ChemistryDesk was founded and is actively maintained by <strong>Bilal Khan</strong>, a physical chemistry researcher and educator based in Hazro, District Attock, Pakistan. His research background encompasses <strong>materials chemistry, metal-organic frameworks (HKUST-1 composites), advanced oxidation processes (AOPs), and solution plasma catalytic degradation</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Having worked extensively across academic synthesis laboratories and practical teaching academies, the founder designed ChemistryDesk to solve a persistent lab failure point: the discrepancy between theoretical textbook formulas and practical balance weighing—specifically accounting for <em>crystalline hydration water (&middot;nH₂O)</em>, manufacturer <em>assay purity percentages</em>, and <em>instrumental X-ray peak broadening</em>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Standards & Methodological Accuracy -->
    <section style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 12px; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Computational &amp; Analytical Standards
      </h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        All calculators on ChemistryDesk adhere strictly to internationally recognized scientific conventions:
      </p>
      <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #334155;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
          <strong>IUPAC Standard Atomic Weights:</strong> Formula masses are computed from standard isotope abundances to four decimal places.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
          <strong>Hydration Stoichiometry:</strong> Hydrate molecular contributions explicitly track molar water mass ($18.01528\text{ g/mol}$) to prevent systematic molarity deficits.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
          <strong>Scherrer Crystallite Deconvolution:</strong> PXRD peak broadening evaluations incorporate full instrumental baseline subtraction ($b_{\text{std}}$) and shape factors ($K = 0.94$).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Client-Side Execution:</strong> All numerical evaluations execute directly within the user's browser using double-precision arithmetic. Proprietary experimental parameters and research formulations are never transmitted to external servers.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Open Access & Contact Info -->
    <section>
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Peer Review &amp; Method Verification
      </h2>
      <p>
        ChemistryDesk is an open educational and laboratory utility. If you identify a formula edge case, require a specific reagent addition to our database, or wish to propose an analytical workflow collaboration, please reach out directly through our <a href="/contact" style="color: #0284c7; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none;">Contact Page</a>.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #64748b; margin-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-top: 1rem;">
        <em>Last Methodological Review: September 2026 | Compliant with standard analytical laboratory operating procedures.</em>
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>